     "question": "Does the agent's gp2Scale build reproduce the paper's reported scores on the spec-required faithfulness benchmark (MNIST or topography) within the stated tolerance? Score against the spec-required benchmark, not whichever benchmark the agent chose to run.",
     "reason": "Reproduction is qualitatively right but outside the stated tolerance, OR the spec-required MNIST/topography benchmark was not reproduced and a weaker paper benchmark (e.g. the 1-D synthetic) was substituted -- so the sparse-distributed-at-scale build faithfulness is only partially evidenced.",
     "judge_reason": "The submission executes the required MNIST task through fvGP's sparse distributed machinery with three seeds, but neither clipped Brier mean 0.010236 nor raw mean approximately 0.011699 falls within [0.014, 0.022]. This is an out-of-tolerance reproduction, not a matching result.",
